@startuml TuiStyleDeferredSurfaces
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
' purpose: the three terminal surfaces left in the old style on purpose, and what each is waiting on
' PLANNED — nothing here is implemented; _spec/_plans/ is exempt from the SPEC-reference rule.
'   the language they would join .... _spec/_conventions/tui-design-language.puml
'   what SHIPPED in that pass ....... _spec/internal/ui/output-vocabulary.puml
'   surface A's boundary ............ _spec/cmd/proveo-entrypoint/prep-process-boundary.puml
'   surface B's already-styled half . _spec/internal/reviewgate/pty-review-proxy.puml
'   the decision both waited on ..... _spec/_plans/retire-dind.puml (APPLIED)
'   what replaces A's seeding ....... _spec/internal/sbx/sbx-kit-contract.puml
'   what replaces B's gate .......... _spec/internal/sbx/policy-baseline.puml
'
' ── WHY THESE TWO WERE HELD BACK ───────────────────────────────────────────
' The host-side status stream joined the design language in one pass because it
' is unambiguously staying: every backend narrates through it. These two do not
' have that property. Both are strongly coupled to the docker backend, and sbx
' is expected to deprecate the mechanism each one decorates. Restyling a surface
' on its way out spends the effort twice — once now, once when its replacement
' needs the same treatment — and, worse, it makes the surface look maintained.
'
' So the ban on emoji is stated for the whole tree and ENFORCED only where it
' has been applied. The contract test carries an explicit exemption list naming
' these files, so the exemption is a fact in the test rather than a gap in it.
'
' ── SURFACE A — THE IN-CONTAINER ENTRYPOINT PREAMBLE ───────────────────────
' cmd/proveo-entrypoint/main.go prints fourteen emoji lines with raw fmt.Printf,
' bypassing internal/ui entirely, plus one in internal/entrypoint. It is the
' agent's own prelude: .env loading, git context, gh session, the smoke
' sentinel. prep-process-boundary calls that the "stdout preamble", and it is
' the one part of prep whose effect is meant to cross the process boundary.
'
' Three things make it a bad first customer. It runs INSIDE the image, so a
' source edit is inert until `proveo build <harness>` — the loop is a rebuild
' per iteration rather than a test run. Its tier cannot be read from the
' operator's PROVEO_GLYPHS unless that variable is deliberately forwarded into
' the container, which is a plumbing decision this pass did not want to make
' quietly. And on the sbx backend most of what it reports is already sbx's job:
' the kit seeds the sandbox, and sbx owns the credential path.
'
' THE DECISION IT WAITS ON. Whether prep survives sbx at all. If the kit
' absorbs the seeding, the preamble does not need a design language — it needs
' deleting, and the facts it prints move to the host stream that already has one.
'
' ── SURFACE C — THE defs/**/*.sh LAYER ─────────────────────────────────────
' Found while scoping the first pass, and the largest of the three by volume:
' 105 emoji lines over 21 shell files. It splits almost in half by WHERE it runs,
' and the halves have different owners.
'
' In-container (~69 lines): the four harness entrypoints — opencode 19, cursor
' 17, claudecode/mcp 11, cecli 10 — plus the mitmproxy and squid sidecar
' scripts. This is surface A again in another language, and it is deferred for
' the same reason: sbx's kit is expected to absorb the seeding, and the two
' sidecars belong to the docker backend that retire-dind has now shrunk to a
' PROVEO_SBX=0 fallback.
'
' Host-side, build time (~30 lines): defs/lib/docker-build.sh, the five build.sh
' and four ensure.sh scripts, defs/lib/egress.sh, run_contract_tests.sh. These
' an operator reads during `proveo build`, so they are squarely in scope by
' locality — and still deferred, because shell cannot import internal/ui. Doing
' them properly means a sourced defs/lib/ui.sh carrying the same six roles, the
' same three tiers and the same marks, which is a vocabulary to design rather
' than a set of strings to swap.
'
' WHAT WAS TRIED AND BACKED OUT. docker-build.sh's pin note was converted to a
' plain "pin: " tag in the first pass and reverted. One converted script among
' twenty-one is worse than none: it reads as the style being applied when it is
' not, and it splits the contract test's exemption list along a line nobody
' chose. internal/contract/agent_pin_test.go asserts that script's output, so it
' carries a surface-C exemption and its expectations move when the script does.
'
' ── SURFACE B — THE LINE-BASED PROMPTS ─────────────────────────────────────
' Three prompts still read a line from stdin instead of drawing a form:
' promptYesNo and promptEnv in cmd/proveo/wizard.go, and provision.go's build
' question, which prefixes itself with a hammer emoji. Note what is NOT in this
' list: the review tier's connection consent already draws through
' choiceui.Consent on a tcell overlay over the suspended PTY, so the hardest
' one of these is conformant today and is the proof the pattern works.
'
' THE DECISION IT WAITED ON. Two, in fact. The review prompts are the docker
' backend's, and retire-dind — now applied — leaves that backend alive only as
' the PROVEO_SBX=0 fallback, so their volume has already fallen to near zero. Separately, a form
' cannot be the only rendering: promptEnv reads SECRETS, and it has to keep
' working with no TTY, in CI, and under a pipe. That means every converted
' prompt needs a headless path anyway, which is a contract worth designing once
' rather than three times.

title PLANNED — three TUI surfaces deferred, and what each waits on

package "joined the language (shipped)" as DONE <<app>> {
  component "internal/ui\nsix roles · three severities\nmeasured, wrapped" as UI <<app>>
  component "~90 host call sites\nrun · sandbox · cmd/proveo\negress · egressproxy · credentials" as SITES <<app>>
  component "internal/choiceui\nthe original speaker" as CUI <<app>>
  component "choiceui.Consent\nreview connection prompt\nalready conformant" as CONSENT <<app>>
}

package "deferred — surface A" as A <<cloud>> {
  component "cmd/proveo-entrypoint/main.go\n14 raw fmt.Printf\nfour emoji, one variation-selected" as EP <<error>>
  component "internal/entrypoint\nPROVEO_SMOKE_READY" as EPL <<error>>
}

package "deferred — surface B" as B <<cloud>> {
  component "wizard.go promptYesNo\npromptEnv — reads secrets" as WIZ <<error>>
  component "provision.go\nthe build question" as PROV <<error>>
}

package "deferred — surface C" as C <<cloud>> {
  component "4 harness entrypoint.sh\n+ 2 sidecar scripts\n~69 lines, in-container" as SHIN <<error>>
  component "docker-build.sh · build.sh ×5\nensure.sh ×4 · egress.sh\n~30 lines, host build time" as SHOUT <<error>>
  component "defs/lib/ui.sh\nsix roles · three tiers\nDOES NOT EXIST" as SHUI <<async>>
}

component "sbx kit contract\nseeds the sandbox" as KIT <<host>>
component "sbx policy baseline\nowns egress decisions" as POL <<host>>
component "retire-dind (APPLIED)\ndocker → PROVEO_SBX=0 fallback" as DIND <<host>>
component "contract test\nexemption list names\nboth surfaces explicitly" as TEST <<async>>

SITES ARROW_MAIN UI
CUI ARROW_MAIN UI : shares the palette
CONSENT ARROW_MAIN CUI
KIT ARROW_ERROR EP : may delete, not restyle
POL ARROW_ERROR WIZ : may retire the question
DIND ARROW_OPTIONAL WIZ : volume fell to the fallback
TEST ARROW_QUEUE A : exempt, by name
TEST ARROW_QUEUE C : exempt, by name
EP ARROW_OPTIONAL UI : where the facts would move
KIT ARROW_ERROR SHIN : may delete, not restyle
SHOUT ARROW_OPTIONAL SHUI : needs a vocabulary first
SHIN ARROW_OPTIONAL SHUI

note bottom of EP
  **Inert until a rebuild.** The images bake the
  entrypoint, so every iteration on this file costs
  ""proveo build <harness>"" rather than ""go test"".
  That alone makes it the wrong surface to iterate a
  design language on — and the reason to decide its
  FATE before its styling.
end note

note bottom of WIZ
  **A form cannot be the only rendering.** ""promptEnv""
  reads secrets and must keep working with no TTY, in
  CI, and under a pipe. Converting three prompts means
  designing one headless contract, not three — which is
  the actual work here, and it is not styling.
end note

note right of TEST
  **The exemption is a fact in the test, not a gap.**
  ""TestNoEmojiReachesTheTerminal"" parses every Go
  string literal under ""internal/"", ""cmd/"" and ""lib/""
  and fails on a rune whose width a terminal and
  ""go-runewidth"" can disagree about. Four files are
  listed by path with the reason each is still allowed
  to print in the old style, so deleting an entry is how
  the work gets picked up and nothing drifts back in
  behind one.

  It does NOT scan shell. Surface C is deferred by
  ABSENCE rather than by exemption, which is the one
  soft edge in this plan: a new emoji in a ""defs/*.sh""
  is caught by nothing. Extending the walk to shell is
  the first commit of surface C's work, before any
  string is swapped.
end note

note bottom of SHUI
  **Shell cannot import internal/ui, so the language has
  to be ported rather than called.** Six roles, three
  tiers, the same marks, and the same rule that severity
  is the glyph and role is the colour — as a sourced
  file, so twenty-one scripts share one copy instead of
  each holding its own ""echo"" prefix. That is the work.
  Swapping 105 strings without it just moves the problem.
end note

note bottom of CONSENT
  **The hard one is already done.** Connection consent
  draws a centred tcell modal through the proveo palette
  over a suspended PTY. Whatever replaces the wizard's
  line prompts has a working precedent to copy.
end note

@enduml
